1. Modified | Function implementation code block
   Replaced the entire body of `raise_ioerror(error)`.
   The original implementation included:

   * Exception-handling structure: call `Image.core.getcodecstatus(error)` to obtain `message`, and use `ERRORS.get(error)` after catching `AttributeError`;
   * Conditional statement: when `message` was empty, set it to `"decoder error %d" % error`;
   * Exception-raising statement: raise `OSError(message + " when reading image file")`.

   The new implementation includes:

   * API call: call `warnings.warn(...)` to issue a `DeprecationWarning`;
   * Return statement: return the result of `raise_oserror(error)`.
